---
import InfoPage from '../../components/InfoPage.astro';

const body = "All subjects follow CBSE guidelines and the NCERT course of study. Students prepare for the CBSE Secondary (Class X) and Senior Secondary (Class XII) board examinations.\n\nTeaching is interactive and uses multimedia aids, group discussions, seminars, guest speakers, field visits and project work. Literary, cultural, sports and computer activities are part of everyday learning, and the school keeps a full record of each student's progress.\n\n### The school year\n\nThe academic session runs from April to March in two terms: April to September, and October to March.\n\n### Kindergarten\n\nKindergarten builds social, emotional and language skills through play, art, dance, music and movement. Children develop communication skills, confidence and creativity, and the early skills for reading, writing and mathematics. Moral stories, puzzles, building blocks and craft such as origami are part of the day.\n\n### XSEED in the primary years\n\nPrimary classes use XSEED, an experiential way of teaching with board-aligned lesson plans. Each lesson moves through five steps:\n\n- **Aim:** be clear about what students should be able to do by the end.\n- **Activity:** children start with an activity and try things out for themselves.\n- **Analyse:** the teacher introduces the concept through questions and discussion.\n- **Apply:** self-study and worksheets with reflective questions and challenging problems.\n- **Assess:** application-based questions check understanding.";
---

<InfoPage
  title="Curriculum"
  description="SBPS follows the CBSE curriculum from Nursery to XII, with XSEED experiential learning in the early years."
